<DocsLayout
  title="Gaming Mode"
  description="Automatic game detection, unique chatter spike counting, and webcam framing for gaming streams."
  currentPath="/docs/gaming-mode"
  section="Gaming Mode"
>
  <h2>1. Automatic Game Recognition</h2>
  <p>
    <code>studio/games.py</code> identifies 23+ games—including GTA VI, GTA V, Fortnite, Minecraft,
    Valorant, Elden Ring, Palworld, Helldivers 2, Marvel Rivals, and Rocket League—from the
    creator's Setup, live stream title, or video filename.
  </p>
  <p>
    When a game is detected, <code>GAME_RULES</code> in <code>studio/brain.py</code> instructs the AI
    to look for plays, clutches, deaths, jump scares, glitches, and reactions, and attaches
    game-specific hashtags automatically.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Counting Unique People in Chat</h2>
  <p>
    Instead of letting one viewer spamming 50 emotes trigger a false hype spike,{" "}
    <code>studio/live.py</code> tracks unique chatters so chat spikes reflect real audience
    reactions.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Facecam Detection</h2>
  <p>
    <code>studio/facecam.py</code> locates static webcam overlays in gaming VODs and streams so
    vertical <code>9:16</code> exports can frame both gameplay and streamer reaction cleanly.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
